hi everyone my name is Sally I'm here at  Q con Barcelona and this morning I gave  a keynote about kubernetes storage my  talk was about debunking the myth that  kubernetes storage is hard one of the  biggest challenges that we have with  storage in general is that really it is  complicated but the beauty of kubernetes  is that it introduces abstraction layers  and when we have these abstraction  layers we can take a very big  complicated problem and break it into  smaller pieces so with kubernetes  storage what we're able to do is treat  storage as four different problems one  you have to figure out what storage you  want to use two you have to figure out  how to deploy that Storage three you  have to figure out how to integrate that  deployed storage with your kubernetes  cluster four you have to figure out how  your containerized workload is going to  consume the deployed storage so to sum  things up storage is complicated but the  reality is that the way we deal with  complicated problems is by breaking them  into smaller pieces and what kubernetes  allows you to do is finally treat  storage as smaller subproblems that you  can handle independently and that  simplifies the overall process of  deploying stateful workloads on  kubernetes so for the full talk take a  look at the description below and stay  tuned for more cute con content  [Music]
 

